    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i'm taking the eurostar from st pancras to paris next week. i have a couple of really heavy suitcases and i'm a bit worried about the check-in process and the bag limits. what are the actual rules for luggage and how early do i really need to be there to get through everything without a massive headache?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the Eurostar, the checked luggage limit is 70kg (154lbs) per item and 100kg (220lbs) per person for excess luggage. You can also bring two additional large extra-cost luggage items. It's recommended to arrive at St Pancras with plenty of time, at least 30-45 minutes, to check-in and collect your pre-checked tickets. For lighter luggage, you can also consider using the unchecked luggage area, which has flexible weight limits.",
      "source": "target",
